{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794414104,"nonce":"jMrQ7XUKzaog9eKFlE5Tx/5/k6I=","message":"Item 2, in part: a function can return `Future\u003cT\u003e`, `Stream\u003cT\u003e` or\n`Signal\u003cT\u003e`, and the Haxe method returns `hxn.Future\u003cT\u003e`, `hxn.Stream\u003cT\u003e` or\n`hxn.Signal\u003cT\u003e`.\n\nHow it is generated (`crates/hxn-gen/src/later.rs`):\n\n- The adapter hands each over as a handle of `AnyFuture`, `AnyStream` or\n  `AnySignal`. Per library, not per function, it exports `outbox_wait` and\n  `outbox_next`; for each kind used, `wait`, `watch` and for a future `state`;\n  and one take a carried type: `future_take_\u003ckind\u003e`, `stream_next_\u003ckind\u003e`,\n  `signal_get_\u003ckind\u003e`.\n- Carried types: `bool`, `i32`, `f64`, `String`. A future or stream can also\n  carry an interface (a shared one as `Arc\u003cT\u003e`), which the taking side owns.\n- Haxe: `Hxn\u003cLibrary\u003eInbox` holds the library's one `hxn.Inbox`, and\n  `Hxn\u003cLibrary\u003eFuture`, `...Stream`, `...Signal` make the objects, with an\n  `of\u003cKind\u003e` a carried type. On hxcpp those classes own the handle and have\n  the finalizer; on HashLink the VM does.\n- An adapter imports `hxn-future` only when the library returns one of\n  these, and `hxn build` adds the dependency to the adapter crate only then.\n- `Result\u003cFuture\u003cT\u003e, E\u003e` is a function that can refuse before there is a\n  future.\n\nFixture: `Later` in `tests/counter/core`, checked by `later()` in\n`Generated.hx`: waits, failures, cancellation, objects and shared objects\narriving later, streams read by iteration and by `listen`, signals followed\nunder `Loop.manual`. Passes on Ash (hybrid, jit, interp, four runs each),\nstock HashLink (five runs), hxcpp (five runs), Ash wasm and hxcpp through\nEmscripten. `hxn run hl` and `hxn run cpp` were tried by hand on a library\nreturning a future.\n\nNot built, still under item 2:\n\n- `async fn`. A receiver or a `\u0026str` borrowed across an await cannot be held\n  by the adapter; the library returns `spawn(async move { ... })` itself.\n- Lent callbacks as parameters, which the hand-written fixture has (`apply`).\n- `Future\u003c()\u003e`, and bytes carried by any of the three.\n- Anything coming the other way: a Haxe-settled future or a Haxe-fed stream\n  is an interface the library writes (`Promise`, `Emitter` in the fixture).\n- Write-through for a signal a binding also sets. The generator cannot know\n  which setter belongs to which signal; the app or a wrapper does it.\n- `hxn_future::Future\u003cT\u003e` written with its path is not recognised, only\n  `Future\u003cT\u003e`.","files":null}]}